    [Feature][KV Transfer] Support GLM-5.3-Flash Mooncake layerwise KV transfer (#17720)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    GLM-5.3-Flash has prefix-cacheable MLA/indexer pages, TP-sharded KDA
    state, and a request-owned K-pool tail. Mooncake layerwise
    initialization rejects the private group even though that state should
    never enter external prefix storage.
    
    Allow private groups with Mooncake block-key layerwise transfer, exclude
    them from hashing and payloads, and load cacheable state at the aligned
    resume boundary so the private tail can be reconstructed locally. Uses
    upstream KDA connector hooks and TP-state ownership/key handling;
    existing MemCache support is preserved.
    
    Only implementation and unit tests are included. No documentation or e2e
    files are changed.
    | Model | Cards | Data Type | Layerwise Enabled | Pooling Enabled |
    Input | Output | External Prefix Cache | Prefix Cache | P Parallel
    Config | D Parallel Config | Concurrency | Total Requests | TTFT (s) |
    TPOT (ms) | Per-Card Output Throughput (tokens/s) |
    | :--- | ---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | :---: |
    :---: | :---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
    | glm5.3-flash | 8 | W8A8 | Yes | Yes | 16k | 1 | 90% | / | TP8EP8 | / |
    32 | 256 | 3.67 | / | 16943 |
    | glm5.3-flash | 8 | W8A8 | No | Yes | 16k | 1 | 90% | / | TP8EP8 | / |
    32 | 256 | 4.05 | / | 15476 |
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. GLM-5.3-Flash can initialize Mooncake block-key layerwise transfer
    with aligned KDA state while keeping its private tail request-local.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - CPU/mock targeted regression tests: 104 passed, 52 subtests passed;
    two tests require unavailable local dependencies.
    - Full remote CPU UT previously reported 9957 passed and one obsolete
    GLM rejection assertion failed on both vLLM versions. That assertion is
    now replaced by initialization and private-group exclusion checks.
    Updated remote results pending.
    - Changed tests pass mypy and Ruff checks locally.
    - Documentation and e2e changes removed at the author's request. The
    main branch contains an unrelated broken GLM5.3.md link to kv_pool.md
    that fails strict RTD builds; fixing that link was verified to pass both
    English and Chinese RTD, but is excluded from this PR.
    - Real Ascend NPU/Mooncake execution remains unverified on this
    development host.
    
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/8cc9aa5ad350f6f80cf3bebb298d410803ff75a9
    
    Signed-off-by: fangrongcan <17343701736@163.com>

